{:eval/lib :liquid-glass-ui, :eval/axis :axis/clarity, :eval/layer :llm-judge, :eval/score 4.50, :eval/judge "llm-judge-1", :eval/run-id "design-quality-20260713-0544", :eval/at "2026-07-13T05:44:03Z", :eval/seq 68, :eval/note "Naming is precise and self-documenting (css-variables/dark-css-variables/resolve-tokens/class-name, namespaced token keys like :liquid-glass/surface), and every public fn has a docstring stating its exact opts and shape (e.g. panel's :surface/:elevation enum, text-field's full attr-passthrough list). Some incidental complexity is unavoidable but well-contained and explained in comments (control-attrs' reagent :on-input->:on-change rewrite for the keystroke-loss bug, the SVG lens token resolution at hiccup-emit time because filter primitives can't read CSS vars). A reader skimming tokens.cljc or components.cljc would understand almost every function's purpose immediately."}
